            "issue": "The note discusses agency versus controlling power for ὑπ’ αὐτοῦ but treats συμπαθείσης as necessarily depicting shared suffering. Its shared-affection or affinity sense is a material alternative here. “Suffers with it” can imply that the demon also suffers, whereas the preceding clauses expressly contrast the soul's torment with the demon's pleasure. The suffering interpretation should not be presented without disclosing and evaluating the shared-condition alternative. This is an interpretive issue, not evidence of defective print.",
